{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>The gate's UI is the whole product</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      An approval gate is only as good as what it actually shows. If the pending action is described vaguely, approval becomes a formality instead of a real check, show the specific, real details every time.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Add a timeout or expiry to pending actions, a stale approval request for a plan based on data that's now an hour old shouldn't still be one click away from executing without re-confirming the underlying state hasn't changed.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Log every approval and rejection with who approved it and the exact parameters shown, this is the audit trail that matters after an incident, not the agent's internal reasoning trace, since the reasoning didn't cause the outcome, the click did.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

